Description: Add support for building System.Security.Cryptography.Native against OpenSSL 4
 Backports the upstream OpenSSL 4.0 compatibility work from dotnet/runtime so the
 native crypto shim builds and runs correctly against both OpenSSL 3.x and the
 upcoming OpenSSL 4.0 series (which removes/deprecates several APIs the shim used
 directly, e.g. direct struct field access on ASN1_STRING, non-const X509_NAME/
 X509_PUBKEY accessors, sk_X509_new_null(), and ENGINE support).
Origin: backport, https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/122744, https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125470, https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125687
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-08-05
